{
 "id": "s4-l7",
 "stage": 4,
 "lesson": 7,
 "title": {
  "de": "Wohin und wo: 에",
  "en": "Where to and where: 에"
 },
 "intro": {
  "de": "에 zeigt das Ziel (wohin?) oder den Ort, an dem etwas ist (wo?). Es bleibt immer gleich, egal ob Vokal oder Konsonant: 공항에 가요, 호텔에 있어요.\nMit 가요, 와요, 있어요 und 없어요 brauchst du fast immer 에.\nDas Fragewort ist 어디 (wo, wohin): 어디에 가요? = Wohin gehst du?",
  "en": "에 marks a destination (where to?) or the place where something is (where?). It never changes, vowel or consonant: 공항에 가요, 호텔에 있어요.\nWith 가요, 와요, 있어요 and 없어요 you almost always need 에.\nThe question word is 어디 (where): 어디에 가요? = Where are you going?"
 },
 "exercises": [
  "see-meaning",
  "pick-hangul",
  "build-sentence"
 ],
